To settle all this, I read the code.  The two columns in question mean
the following:

First column: to-hit bonus maximum

Second column: damage bonus maximum, except when it's "x2" which doubles
damage in all cases

Both are implemented by generating a random number between 1 and the
given value and adding that to some total that is being added up.
These are apparently the same sums discussed in the spoilers, the first
for hit probability and the second for amount of damage.

As far as I can tell, there is nothing special done about the damage
bonus vs. small/medium/large monsters.  However, this part of the code
is very convoluted.

I also checked the version of the random number routine that is used
(there are several) and 1 is indeed the minimum value.  So you always
get at least 1 bonus point, except for Snickersnee's to-hit bonus which
is always 0.  Of course, Snickersnee already has another to-hit bonus
figured elsewhere for being a katana.

For the technically-oriented, these numbers are the attk.damn and
attk.damd fields in the artifact structure.


